   DEGRADED: production runs PostgreSQL 17.x. This run is 16.13 (Ubuntu 16.13-0ubuntu0.24.04.1), so it proves the DDL,
   the behaviour, the idempotency and the restore path but NOT 17.x-specific behaviour.
   Every statement here (DROP INDEX IF EXISTS, ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS, CREATE UNIQUE
   INDEX IF NOT EXISTS, and the DO-block guards) is invariant across 11-17 — but the
   17.6 run is CI's `migrations` job on the pull request, not this script.
   PostgreSQL 17.6 was not obtainable in the authoring session: only 16.x is installed,
   the Docker daemon is unavailable (/var/run/docker.sock absent), and apt.postgresql.org
   is policy-denied by the egress proxy (403). Recorded rather than approximated.

